Drop active values
	
	An active value whose usage is set as "drop site" names a target accepted 
	by the widget as a drop site. You will define the set script for the target.
	It  should read the data received in the @ argument, and 
	use it as needed. Clicking on the ellipsis opens an edit box for multi-
	line scripts.
	
	The box has the following fields:
	
	"Usage"  Specify the usage for the active value.
	
	"Drop Targets" This box lists the targets specified as drop sites for 
	the selected widget. 
	
	"Drop Target Name" Specify the name of a target accepted by the 
	selected widget as a drop site. 
	
	"List..." Pops up the Drop Target Selector.
	Select a drop site from a 
	list of commonly accepted selection targets as defined in the "Inter-Client 
	Communication Convention Manual" by the X Consortium.
	Selecting one enters it in the "Drop Target Name" field. 
	"A list of active values"  Only active values that have the same usage appear in 
	this field, if you are using "new style" active values (version 3.0 
	and later). However, older .fm files with "old style" active values will 
	display all the active values of the widget, regardless of their usage.
	
	"Custom Editor"  Opens the editor you specified using the FMEDITOR environment variable. 
	
	"Clear" Clears the editing field.
	
	"Get/Set Script"  Enter get and set scripts for the active value. By 
	convention, the get script updates the active value's data to reflect the 
	interface's current setting. The set script tells the interface that the 
	data has changed so that the interface can change its presentation.
	
	"Add" Defines the active value for the current widget and registers the changes.
	
	"Replace"  Replaces the active value selected  in the display box with the newly
	defined active value.
	
	"Delete" Deletes the selected active value and its get and set scripts.
	
	The "up" and "down" arrows move the selected active value one position
	up or down in the active values list.
	
	"Close"  Closes the  window. If you have added (by clicking 
	on the Add button) an active value to the widget you are editing, the 
	active value is applied to the widget. If not, clicking Close merely closes 
	the window without changing the widget.
		
